  "evidence_tier": 1,
  "evidence": "Tier 1 (executed differential) for MRMAssay::reannotateTransitions (2 parameter sets), restrictTransitions (without and with the class test's 32 swathes), detectingTransitions, filterMinMaxTransitionsCompound, filterUnreferencedDecoysCompound, uisTransitions (all 5 class-test parameter sets, seed 42) and MRMDecoy::generateDecoys (pseudo-reverse as the class test, reverse, fraction 0.5, switchKR), and through them MRMIonSeries::getIonSeries, annotateIon, getIon and annotateTransitionCV, on the class-test TraML inputs: driver ../oracle/O1c-assays/driver.cpp built with x86_64-conda-linux-gnu-g++ 14.4.0 -O3 -DNDEBUG against the Linux x86-64 Release install /ceph/ibmi/abi/oliver/opt/openms4-release-bc9cc12-c19e494-174b576 (libOpenMS.so sha256 abd4fc9977823c793b4396586210a867cf72482cd3ab228d6aec8ddb54966d6c) on ibminode06, every case run twice in fresh processes with byte-identical stdout, stderr and exit (results/differ.txt empty), and the whole batch run twice with identical case hashes. Every compared field matches exactly except the unrounded decoy precursor m/z, within a declared 4-ulp relative tolerance whose cause (residue internal masses summed in a different element order) the decoy_masses case pins. Tier 3 (source review) for every literal of MRMIonSeries_test.cpp, MRMDecoy_test.cpp (all seeded shuffles, reversals, identity, switchKR, terminal-modification checks, the heavy duplicate-detection regression) and MRMAssay_test.cpp (matching peptidoforms, swath lookup, random sequence, n-choose-k, addModificationsSequences, 13 theoretical peptidoforms, decoy peptidoforms). Tier 4 for the native checks.",
